# MAVLink stream rates for the companion-computer link.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `MavlinkTelemetry` is read-only by construction: it has no method that can
# transmit, and tests assert that. A normal ground station opens a link and then
# *asks* for data with REQUEST_DATA_STREAM or SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL. This
# companion cannot, so ArduPilot sends it heartbeats and nothing else, and every
# snapshot comes back empty -- lat None, fix_type 0, hdop 99.9. Which is the
# correct representation of "no data", and looks exactly like a broken decoder.
#
# The resolution is not to make the link writable. It is that the autopilot is
# configured to stream, once, at setup -- which is how the real aircraft will be
# built too. The companion listens; the autopilot talks; neither needs the other
# to ask.
#
# SERIAL0 is what scripts/sitl.sh connects to, so these are the SR0_ rates. On
# the real airframe, set the SRx_ block for whichever port the Pi is wired to
# (SERIAL1 or SERIAL2 on a Pixhawk) with the same values.
#
# Rates are in Hz. They are deliberately modest: the pipeline captures at 1 Hz
# and gates on telemetry no older than 2 s, so 4-5 Hz gives margin without
# filling a 57600-baud radio link. Raise EXTRA1 if attitude at capture matters
# more than bandwidth.

# GPS fix, satellites, HDOP -- the GNSS gate reads all three.
SR0_EXT_STAT     4

# Position: GLOBAL_POSITION_INT, the lat/lon/alt every detection is placed by.
SR0_POSITION     4

# Attitude: roll/pitch/yaw. The 10-degree nadir gate reads this, so it wants to
# be at least as fast as the capture rate.
SR0_EXTRA1       5

# VFR_HUD: groundspeed, which the motion-blur budget is computed against.
SR0_EXTRA2       4

# Battery and system status.
SR0_EXTRA3       2

# Raw IMU and RC are not read by anything in this pipeline. Left at zero rather
# than "low": an unused stream is bandwidth taken from one that is used.
SR0_RAW_SENS     0
SR0_RC_CHAN      0
SR0_RAW_CTRL     0
SR0_PARAMS       0
